 et al. [11] : to reconcile the predicted number of jetted quasars with the overall number of quasars expected from the UV luminosity function is that all quasars host jets, including very weak ones that remain undetectable with current radio surveys (a hypothesis also mentioned by e.g., Sbarrato et al. 98 , Wolf et al. 127 ). Pushing the detection threshold of radio follow-up observations to ≤ 1 ​ μ \leq 1\,\mu Jy should therefore enable the detection of jets in essentially all quasars. Figure 3: Allowed values of the jet viewing angle ( θ 	heta ) and left panel : bulk velocity in units of the speed of light ( β = v / c  eta=v/c ), right panel : the bulk Lorentz factor ( Γ \Gamma ). The red shaded area corresponds to the allowed parameter space in the β − θ  eta-	heta and Γ − θ \Gamma-	heta plane for the inferred δ > 19.3 \delta>19.3 . Curves for other values of δ \delta are shown for comparison.

